; A step's A and a coefficient K (k = K/1000) in, the five cards a lattice machine's multiply routine is made of
; out: the sign word (ADD t or SUB t, t being cell 86 in every lattice machine), the jumps into the row of ADDs for
; k's second and first digits (JMP 99-d), SFT 0L, and the rounding half, 5 x 10^(L-1), or 0 when A is 0, so that in
; a pause the lattice truncates toward zero and dies away instead of holding a small tone. k keeps two digits from
; its first one, L: L is 1 for |K| from 100, 2 from 10, 3 below; for L = 1 the second digit is rounded, and 0.995
; and up stay 0.99.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            loop    INP   a        03-15: the step's A and K, the sign word, and m = |K|
  04                    INP   k
  05                    CLA   k
  06                    TAC   neg
  07                    CLA   wadd
  08                    STO   sw
  09                    CLA   k
  10                    JMP   mag
  11            neg     CLA   wsub
  12                    STO   sw
  13                    CLA   z
  14                    SUB   k
  15            mag     STO   m
  16                    SUB   c100     16-30: L = 1, n = (m + 5) / 10, at most 99
  17                    TAC   small
  18                    CLA   m
  19                    ADD   five
  20                    SFT   01
  21                    STO   n
  22                    SUB   c100
  23                    TAC   l1
  24                    CLA   c99
  25                    STO   n
  26            l1      CLA   f401
  27                    STO   fin
  28                    CLA   five
  29                    STO   h
  30                    JMP   out
  31            small   CLA   m        31-40: L = 2, n = m
  32                    SUB   ten
  33                    TAC   l3
  34                    CLA   m
  35                    STO   n
  36                    CLA   f402
  37                    STO   fin
  38                    CLA   fifty
  39                    STO   h
  40                    JMP   out
  41            l3      CLA   m        41-47: L = 3, n = 10 m
  42                    SFT   10
  43                    STO   n
  44                    CLA   f403
  45                    STO   fin
  46                    CLA   c500
  47                    STO   h
  48            out     OUT   sw       48-70: the five cards; SFT 33 keeps n's last digit, SFT 01 drops it
  49                    CLA   n
  50                    SFT   33
  51                    STO   d
  52                    CLA   c899
  53                    SUB   d
  54                    STO   d
  55                    OUT   d
  56                    CLA   n
  57                    SFT   01
  58                    STO   d
  59                    CLA   c899
  60                    SUB   d
  61                    STO   d
  62                    OUT   d
  63                    OUT   fin
  64                    CLA   z        the rounding half, or 0 (truncation) in a step with A = 0
  65                    SUB   a
  66                    TAC   rnd
  67                    OUT   z
  68                    JMP   loop
  69            rnd     OUT   h
  70                    JMP   loop
  71            k       DATA  0
  72            sw      DATA  0
  73            m       DATA  0
  74            n       DATA  0
  75            fin     DATA  0
  76            h       DATA  0
  77            d       DATA  0
  78            z       DATA  0
  79            wadd    ADD   86
  80            wsub    SUB   86
  81            c100    DATA  100
  82            c99     DATA  99
  83            five    DATA  5
  84            ten     DATA  10
  85            fifty   DATA  50
  86            c500    DATA  500
  87            c899    DATA  899
  88            f401    SFT   01
  89            f402    SFT   02
  90            f403    SFT   03
  91            a       DATA  0
